<p class="hint">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms; they are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice. Default figures are illustrative.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>How depreciation is calculated here</h2>
<p>The calculator uses straight-line depreciation — age divided by expected life — capped at the maximum you choose. Real estimates may use condition adjustments, different life expectancies or non-depreciable items such as permits and some labor, so treat the result as a planning figure.</p>
<h2>Island-specific life expectancy questions</h2>
<p>Salt air, strong UV and constant humidity shorten the life of some materials and lengthen arguments about others. Carriers sometimes apply heavy depreciation to metal roofing, window units or exterior paint near the shoreline. Ask how the life expectancy was chosen and whether it reflects the actual material installed.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Range often seen in estimates</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Architectural shingles</th><td>25–30 years</td></tr><tr><th>Painted metal roof panels</th><td>30–50 years</td></tr><tr><th>Interior paint</th><td>8–12 years</td></tr><tr><th>Vinyl plank flooring</th><td>15–25 years</td></tr><tr><th>Window or split AC units</th><td>10–15 years</td></tr><tr><th>Water heater</th><td>8–15 years</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Ranges are general and illustrative, not a standard any carrier must use.</p>
<h2>Getting holdback released</h2>
<p>Most policies release recoverable depreciation once repairs are finished within a time limit. Send invoices and photos of completed work, and calendar the deadline with the <a href="/island-claim-tools/claim-timeline-builder/">claim timeline builder</a>.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can labor be depreciated?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Practice varies by policy and jurisdiction. Ask the carrier to explain in writing whether and how labor was depreciated in your estimate.</p></div></details><details><summary>What happens if I don’t rebuild?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Under most replacement cost policies you keep the actual cash value payment but may not collect the depreciation that was held back.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="related"><a href="/island-claim-tools/roof-pitch-squares-estimator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Roof Pitch &amp; Squares Estimator</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/island-claim-tools/hurricane-deductible-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Hurricane Deductible Calculator</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/island-claim-tools/claim-timeline-builder/"><small>Planner</small><span>Claim Timeline Builder</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/